/-!
# Frobenius fixed points

Source: Weil conjectures blueprint, `thm-trf-frobenius-fixed-points` (blueprint:
thm-trf-frobenius-fixed-points).

The theorem states the scheme-theoretic fixed-point decomposition, its finite étale and
local properties, the tangent differential, and the smooth-locus transverse intersection
and Tor multiplicity clauses.  The fixed scheme is the recorded equalizer construction.
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option warn.sorry false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

namespace WeilConjectures

/-- Scheme-theoretic fixed points of iterated scheme Frobenius over a finite field.

Source: blueprint main-20261015, `sec-six-functors-basics`,
`sk-prop-sf-rf-shriek-preservation/thm-trf-frobenius-fixed-points.proof.md`, Steps 0--3;
the DAG's nine expanded proof steps, especially the smooth-locus qualification in steps 8--9;
Stacks Project, Tag 0B1I, `intersection-lemma-transversal`
(blueprint: thm-trf-frobenius-fixed-points).

Proof plan (the numbered steps are those of the DAG):
1. Choose a finite affine cover of the model using def-weil-finite-type-morphism.
   Frobenius preserves each chart since its map on model primes is the identity.
   The equalizer of def-trf-fixed-scheme on the geometric chart Spec B is Spec(B/J),
   where J is generated by phi(b)-b, by the affine spectrum and fibre-product descriptions.
2. Present the model algebra as k₀[t₁,...,tᵣ]/a. Set Q=q^m. Frobenius fixes k and
   sends each model coordinate to its Q-th power. The difference ideal is generated by
   tᵢ^Q-tᵢ: expand model polynomials, telescope products and use c^Q=c for c in k₀.
3. The unique-subfield lemma identifies the Q distinct roots of T^Q-T with F_Q.
   PolynomialDistinctLinearCRT, iterated over the coordinates, gives the evaluation
   decomposition indexed by F_Q^r; for r=0 there is one empty tuple.
4. In this finite product of fields every ideal is the product of its coordinate ideals,
   by multiplication by coordinate idempotents. Quotienting by a retains exactly the
   tuples satisfying all model relations, namely the extensionPoints. The finite affine
   coproduct-spectrum identification gives the chart isomorphism, also for no points.
5. On overlaps the summand maps are the same scalar-extended rational points, so the
   chart isomorphisms and their inverses glue. The finite chart cover proves that the
   global point index is finite. No separatedness assumption is needed.
6. A finite product of copies of k is finite as a k-module, and the coproduct is étale
   by lem-exc-etale-coproduct-etale. Every fixed stalk is k with its given scalar map;
   its only submodules are zero and itself, giving Module.length one.
7. On model coordinates a dual-number vector has values lambdaᵢ+vᵢ epsilon. Its
   Q-th powers are lambdaᵢ, since Q is a positive characteristic power and epsilon²=0.
   Thus the tangent differential is zero, even at singular fixed points. The product
   tangent space is T_x X × T_x X. The graph and diagonal ranges are (v,0) and (v,v),
   which are complementary since (a,b)=(a-b,0)+(b,b); also 1-dPhi^m is the identity.
8. Only now assume a smooth open U at the fixed point. Choose affine neighbourhoods
   W⊆V⊆U with Phi^m(W)⊆V. Open restriction, the smooth-affine equivalence, base
   change and composition make W×_k V smooth. Its graph and diagonal quotient rings
   are regular local of dimension d, while the ambient stalk A has dimension 2d.
   The graph ideals are exactly the kernels of the two stalk maps. Their sum is the
   maximal ideal, because the intersection stalk is the previously computed k.
9. RegularLocalQuotientKernelParameters chooses parameters generating the graph ideal I.
   RegularLocalGeneratorsRegularSequence gives d generators, regular both on A and A/J.
   RegularSequenceKoszulRegular makes the finite free Koszul resolution acyclic in
   positive degrees before and after tensoring with A/J. Hence Tor₀ is k and Torᵢ=0
   for i>0, by def-weil-pbc-tor-modules, as in Stacks 0B1I. The displayed stronger
   vanishing-and-length form implies the alternating Serre length sum is one: its
   only nonzero term is degree zero, with sign +1. When d=0 both lists are empty.

The two tangent ranges are spanned over the ambient residue field, after transporting
along hx. This is exactly their range subspace: schemeTangentMap is linear over the
source residue field and heG/heΔ identify it isomorphically with the ambient one.
The witnesses hx, heG and heΔ assert canonical point equality and residue bijections;
they do not allow choices of tangent subspaces or ideals. -/
theorem frobenius_fixed_points
    (D : FiniteFieldDatum.{u})
    (X₀ : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of D.k₀)))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType X₀.hom] [QuasiCompact X₀.hom]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 1 ≤ m) :
    let X := D.geometricFiber X₀
    let h : X ⟶ X :=
      Over.homMk (D.schemeFrobeniusIterate X₀ m) (by
        revert hm
        induction m with
        | zero => intro hm; simp [FiniteFieldDatum.schemeFrobeniusIterate, X]
        | succ m ih =>
          intro hm
          cases m with
          | zero =>
            simpa [FiniteFieldDatum.schemeFrobeniusIterate,
              FiniteFieldDatum.schemeFrobenius, X] using
              (FiniteFieldDatum.relativeFrobenius_projections D X₀).2
          | succ m =>
            let Φ : End X.left := D.schemeFrobenius X₀
            have ih' : (Φ ^ (Nat.succ m)) ≫ X.hom = X.hom := by
              simpa [FiniteFieldDatum.schemeFrobeniusIterate, Φ] using ih (by omega)
            have hΦ : Φ ≫ X.hom = X.hom := by
              simpa [Φ, X, FiniteFieldDatum.schemeFrobenius] using
                (FiniteFieldDatum.relativeFrobenius_projections D X₀).2
            change (Φ ^ (Nat.succ (Nat.succ m))) ≫ X.hom = X.hom
            rw [pow_succ]
            simp [Category.assoc, ih', hΦ])
    let F := trfEndomorphismFixedScheme X h
    ∃ e : F ≅ ∐ fun _ : D.extensionPoints X₀ m hm => Spec (.of D.k),
      (Finite (D.extensionPoints X₀ m hm) ∧
        IsFinite (trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h ≫ X.hom) ∧
        Etale (trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h ≫ X.hom)) ∧
      (∀ y : D.extensionPoints X₀ m hm,
        (Sigma.ι (fun _ : D.extensionPoints X₀ m hm => Spec (.of D.k)) y ≫
            e.inv ≫ trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h ≫ X.hom = 𝟙 (Spec (.of D.k))) ∧
        (Sigma.ι (fun _ : D.extensionPoints X₀ m hm => Spec (.of D.k)) y ≫
            e.inv ≫ trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h ≫
            pullback.fst X₀.hom
              (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap D.k₀ D.k))) =
          Scheme.Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (D.extensionSubfield m hm).subtype).op ≫ y.left)) ∧
      (∀ z : F,
        ∃ e₀ : F.presheaf.stalk z ≅ CommRingCat.of D.k,
          (StructureSheaf.toStalk D.k ((trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h ≫ X.hom) z) ≫
            (trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h ≫ X.hom).stalkMap z) ≫ e₀.hom =
              𝟙 (CommRingCat.of D.k) ∧
          Module.length (F.presheaf.stalk z) (F.presheaf.stalk z) = 1) ∧
      (∀ x : X.left, h.left x = x →
        ∀ he : Function.Bijective (h.left.residueFieldMap x).hom,
          AlgebraicGeometry.schemeTangentMap D.k X.left X.left X.hom X.hom h.left
            (by exact Over.w h) x he = 0) ∧
      (∀ (x : F) (U : X.left.Opens),
        trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h x ∈ U → Smooth (U.ι ≫ X.hom) →
        let x' := trfEndomorphismFixedInclusion X h x
        let P := pullback X.hom X.hom
        let pP := pullback.fst X.hom X.hom ≫ X.hom
        let g := trfFixedGraphMap X h
        let δ := pullback.diagonal X.hom
        ∃ (hx : δ x' = g x')
          (heG : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap x').hom)
          (heΔ : Function.Bijective (δ.residueFieldMap x').hom),
          let tG := schemeTangentMap D.k X.left P X.hom pP g
            (by
              dsimp [g, pP, trfFixedGraphMap]
              rw [← Category.assoc, pullback.lift_fst]
              exact Category.id_comp _) x' heG
          let tΔ := schemeTangentMap D.k X.left P X.hom pP δ
            (by
              dsimp [δ, pP]
              rw [← Category.assoc, pullback.diagonal_fst]
              exact Category.id_comp _) x' heΔ
          let G := Submodule.span (P.residueField (g x')) (Set.range tG)
          let Δ := Submodule.span (P.residueField (g x'))
            ((fun v ↦ Eq.mp (congrArg (schemeTangentSpace D.k P pP) hx) v) '' Set.range tΔ)
          let A := P.presheaf.stalk (g x')
          let I := RingHom.ker (g.stalkMap x').hom
          let J := RingHom.ker
            ((P.presheaf.stalkCongr (by rw [hx]; exact Inseparable.rfl)).hom ≫ δ.stalkMap x').hom
          (∃ W : P.Opens, g x' ∈ W ∧ Smooth (W.ι ≫ pP)) ∧
          G ⊔ Δ = ⊤ ∧ G ⊓ Δ = ⊥ ∧
          Module.length A
            (((CategoryTheory.Tor' (ModuleCat A) 0).obj
              (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ J))) = 1 ∧
          ∀ i : ℕ, 0 < i →
            IsZero (((CategoryTheory.Tor' (ModuleCat A) i).obj
              (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I))).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ J)))) := by
  sorry

end WeilConjectures
